Do note that Barbarians aren't all that mentally oriented....

:3. Must sacrifices only be done with fresh meat? I ran across a
:neutral altar (I was a chaotic barbarian) and tried to #offer a jackal
:corpse (possibly old), and "nothing happens" resulted. I then #prayed
:and was told that God Foo-bar was pleased with me. I then #offerred &
:#prayed, doing this about 6 times in a row but nothing visible seemed
:to happen. Should I have continued? Another time I was told that the
:power of Morrigan decreased (sob).
     The Gods are almost, but not quite, as finicky eaters as you are. 
Do note that they get annoyed if you bother them often enough.  And,
while it is unlucky to have the power of your God decrease, it is not
calamitous.  (BTW, use : to determine what God an altar is to.) 
Offering, as you might guess, pleases the Gods, but don't rush the
affair.  Only bother your God when you need to, unless you haven't done
it for a long time anyway and don't forsee needing to in the near
future.

:4. In general when you find lots of armor should you don whatever you
:can? Like +0 elven cloak, a black cap (+0 something else etc.), or
:just stick to your best armor only. 
     Wearing any unidentified piece of armor can be dangerous; do take
advantage of the superstition of your pets!  The AC stat on your screen
will determine how effective your armor is.  In regard to the AC number:
less is more!

:5. Should you just sell all extra stuff to shopkeepers?
