:6. In general should you steal from a shopkeeper? THe only way I can
:think of is to dig a trap door, but doesn't that abandon your pet at
:that level (or will he fall down with you if he is next to you when
:you begin digging)? In general, I have found it better to just wait
:till my pet fleeces most everything from the shop (I pick it all up
:and keep it handy near the door).
     There is a way, with a pickaxe, to ferret stuff off.  This is an
outright spoiler, so I'll put ^Ls on either side:

     Dig two holes in the walls (you can dig through with a pickaxe by
simply repeating the effort until it works) like so:
        # ----b--
        # | )))a| 
        ##-@))))     
          | ))))|# <-- c
          -------
     Pile what you want to steal at (a).  Stand at (b) and kick the
stuff into (c) (which you may have to dig; this technique is somewhat
more convenient if you can easily link (c) to a passage, but that's
unnecessary.  Kicking potions and mirrors will cost you money and get
you nothing in particular.  Anyway, you can pick the stuff up at (c). 
The shopkeeper won't notice.  This scam, apart from training your pet,
is about the only way to steal from a shop without getting the Kops on
your kase.


